From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapi, msttsengine, windows.media.speech: A voice per language, each speaking its own (9418)

There was one voice, English: a program choosing its voice by language
(SAPI's "Language=407", SpeechSynthesizer.AllVoices) found none for
German, and German text through it came out in English sounds.

Each language the engine's synthesizer (eSpeak NG) speaks now has a voice
token, with Language, Name, Gender and Age attributes; the engine reads
its token's language and speaks it for text that names none; and with no
choice of the user's, the default voice is the one of the display
language, as on Windows (SAPI's default token, WinRT's DefaultVoice). An
English display keeps "Wine Default Voice" as the default.
---
